From 55dbf1daa1a9798eb8b922309e290fbb57709b45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:47:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 131/135] media: qcom: camss: csiphy-3ph: add SM8450 C-PHY lane
 settings

Add C-PHY lane settings for SM8450-class CSIPHYs (SM8450, SM8475,
SM7475) so the C-PHY support can be used there. The register values are
the 3-phase lane settings and the data-rate dependent settings for the
1.7 Gsps (3.876 Gbps) and 2.5 Gsps (5.7 Gbps) entries of the Qualcomm
camera kernel CSIPHY v2.1.3 table (cam_csiphy_2_1_3_hwreg.h). The table
is chosen from the link frequency (half the symbol rate). The D-PHY
settings of the same file match the existing X1E80100 table apart from
skew calibration and do-not-program entries.

As in that driver, C-PHY uses the vendor settle count (6 ns in 200 ps
units), common control 7 = 0x7a, and releases the 3-phase reset with
common control 0 = 0x0e followed by 3 ms. The order (common, data-rate,
lane settings, reset release) and the 100 us delays follow the vendor
sequence.

Source: Qualcomm camera kernel CAMERA.LA.2.0.r2-06400-WAIPIO.0 as merged in
https://github.com/Pzqqt/android_kernel_xiaomi_marble/blob/1e2c9406f2b5402a0a2a2bcf89207245299e0fa4/techpack/camera/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_csiphy/include/cam_csiphy_2_1_3_hwreg.h

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 .../qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c         | 263 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 263 insertions(+)

